{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The area of one of the bases of a right circular cylinder is <math alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn>\n</math> square centimeters, and the volume of the cylinder is <math alttext=\"2,187\"><mn>2,187</mn>\n</math> cubic centimeters. What is the height, in centimeters, of the cylinder?</p>", "keys": ["d871b930-33c2-4645-82f2-002eec41d2d1"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "d871b930-33c2-4645-82f2-002eec41d2d1", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "34da11a8-7494-42b2-b35c-f7ea0620b153", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"2,025\"><mn>2,025</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "1f07f2a9-1a12-4b45-9400-bdebe3649406", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"2,106\"><mn>2,106</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "fa2f5a65-b45d-49c6-bfca-9313f9168c11", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"177,147\"><mn>177,147</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a right circular cylinder is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals pi r squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"pi r squared\"><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is the area of one of the bases of the cylinder and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height. It&rsquo;s given that the area of one of the bases of the cylinder is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn></math> square centimeters and that the volume of the cylinder is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,187\"><mn>2,187</mn></math> cubic centimeters. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,187\"><mn>2,187</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"pi r squared\"><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals pi r squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2,187 equals 81 h\"><mn>2,187</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>81</mn><mi>h</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27 equals h\"><mn>27</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>. Therefore, the height, in centimeters, of the cylinder is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "a6f2f98a-1452-4d23-aa35-d397a85c694f", "correct_answer": ["A"]}